# What `make deploy` must not ship to Cloud Build.
#
# Without this file gcloud derives the upload set from .gitignore, which
# is tuned for what should not be *committed* — a different question from
# what belongs in a build context. The gap let three things through:
# worktrees (full copies of this repo, living inside it), local media,
# and secrets.
#
# The Docker build context is this tarball, and the Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .`, so everything excluded here is excluded from the image too.
# Keep go.mod, go.sum, cmd/ and internal/ — that is the entire build.

.git/
.gitignore

# Claude Code keeps worktrees under .claude/, each a full checkout of
# this repository. Uploading them nearly doubled the tarball and put
# stale copies of the codebase in the build context.
.claude/
.agents/

# Local development store: episodes, audio, covers, users.
data/

# Media worked on locally. Root-anchored on purpose: nothing under cmd/
# is an image today, but if an asset is ever embedded it must not vanish
# from the build because of a pattern written years earlier.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.mp3

# Credentials. None of this belongs in an image build context, and some
# of it does not belong on disk either.
.env
.env.*
client_secret*.json
*-key.json
*.pem

# Scratch output from admin endpoints and local experiments.
/costs.json
/costs-episodes.json
/dsm-alice.json
/ft-alice.json
/skills-lock.json

# An alternate image that the deploy does not build.
Dockerfile.opencode
